## Naming Conventions

**N-1. Paths.** New files and directories use lowercase kebab-case. Keep Next.js reserved names (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `route.ts`) and bracketed dynamic segments. Do not opportunistically rename established exceptions such as `src/components/home/CardColumns.tsx`.

**N-2. Symbols.** React components, classes, exported types/interfaces, and Zod schemas use PascalCase. Hooks begin with `use`. Functions, properties, and variables use camelCase. Module constants use descriptive UPPER_SNAKE_CASE when they are true constants.

**N-3. Tests and stories.** Tests use `*.test.ts(x)`. App tests are colocated; worker engine tests live in `workers/game/src/__tests__/`. Stories use `*.stories.tsx` in the feature's existing `__stories__/` convention.

**N-4. APIs.** Resource path segments are plural and kebab-case unless an existing domain contract says otherwise. Dynamic parameters use brackets. Route handler exports are uppercase HTTP verbs.

**N-5. Data.** Prisma models/enums use PascalCase and fields use camelCase; retain explicit `@map`/`@@map` database names. Migration directories use the existing timestamped snake-case form.

**N-6. Cards and engine.** Effect schema filenames are lowercase set IDs (`op16.ts`, `st30.ts`); canonical card IDs and discriminated-union values remain uppercase.
